### Step 10 — Teach the LiveKit token endpoint about the user

Your `temp/.env.example` already carries `LIVEKIT_URL` / `LIVEKIT_API_KEY` / `LIVEKIT_API_SECRET`, so
when `src/routes/api/token/+server.ts` is written, it must:

~~~ts
const { user } = await locals.safeGetSession();
if (!user) error(401, 'not authenticated');

// identity must come from the validated server-side user, never from the request body
const identity = user.id;
const name = user.user_metadata?.display_name ?? user.email ?? 'guest';
~~~

*Why:* the LiveKit access token grants publish/subscribe rights. If `identity` or the room list comes
from client input, any logged-in user can impersonate another participant or join a room they were
never invited to. The `webapp/src/routes/api/token/+server.ts` endpoint is the reference pattern.

